er, String, Table, TypeDecorator, create_engine, func\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.dialects import postgresql\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.declarative import declarative_base\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import backref, contains_eager, joinedload, relationship, sessionmaker\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.sql.type_api import INDEXABLE\r\n\r\nBase = declarative_base()\r\nengine = create_engine(\"postgresql://postgres@localhost:5435/postgres?sslmode=prefer\", echo=True)\r\n\r\n\r\nclass SkipsFirst(TypeDecorator):\r\n    impl = postgresql.ARRAY(Integer, zero_indexes=True)\r\n\r\n    cache_ok = True\r\n\r\n    def process_bind_param(self, value, dialect):\r\n        return value[1:]\r\n\r\n    def copy(self, **kw):\r\n        return SkipsFirst(**kw)\r\n\r\n    def coerce_compared_value(self, op, value):\r\n        return self.impl.coerce_compared_value(op, value)\r\n\r\n\r\nclass Item(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = \"item\"\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n    content = Column(SkipsFirst)\r\n\r\n\r\nBase.metadata.drop_all(engine)\r\nBase.metadata.create_all(engine)\r\nSession = sessionmaker(engine)\r\nsession = Session()\r\n\r\nsession.add(Item(content=[1, 2, 3]))\r\nsession.flush()\r\nprint(session.query(Item.content[0]).all())\r\n```\r\n\r\nI have this error\r\n\r\n```\r\nraise NotImplementedError(NotImplementedError: Operator 'getitem' is not supported on this expression\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe only thing that seems to work is making SkipsFirst subclass INDEXABLE.\r\n\r\n```python\r\nclass SkipsFirst(TypeDecorator, INDEXABLE):\r\n  ...\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis doesn't seem to be coherent with the `TypeDecorator` philosophy. So I don't know if there is a canonical way to still have all the feature of `postgresql.ARRAY`.\n\n### Databases / Backends / Drivers targeted\n\nPostgreSQL in this case but all databases could be concerned.\n\n### Example Use\n\n...\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"htt